            <ArticleTitle>Rectus sheath haematoma associated with low molecular weight heparin: a case series.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>309-12</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A report of three cases of spontaneous rectus sheath haematoma within a 1-month period in a single hospital. The common feature was the recent treatment with low molecular weight heparin. In contrast to the perceived benign nature of the classically-described haematoma, the cases described were life-threatening and required aggressive intervention.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
